CORE
unknown.sh
--unwind 4 --shell-max-arguments 2 --shell-strings native --cvc5
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[assertion\.1\] .*: SUCCESS$
^\[assertion\.2\] .*: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
With arguments not known during conversion, getopts yields the letters
of the option string or "?", and ends with "?". The loop may run more
often than the unwinding bound.
